Everything works. Summary of what changed:

**`src/lib.rs`** — Added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match on each element of `tags` (not substring), order preserved.

**`src/main.rs`** — The `list` command now scans args after the command for a `--tag <TAG>` flag (positional, wherever it appears), and filters through `filter_by_tag` when present; otherwise it lists all.

Verified:
- `cargo build` and `cargo test` pass (existing tests unaffected).
- CLI end-to-end: `list --tag rust` / `--tag world` return the correct subset in original order; an unknown tag yields an empty list; no `--tag` behaves as before.

One design note: the flag is positional (e.g. `notekeep list --tag rust`), consistent with the existing subcommand-style CLI. I did not add a `--tag=rust` form.


